{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuimQgrGpDrQrq8YBVmU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't find an official one. My search turned up no Cloudflare CLI or terminal chat client for the Agents SDK. What exists is client libraries: React hooks such as `useAgentChat` from `@cloudflare/ai-chat`, and a plain `AgentClient` class in `agents/client` that connects to an agent by name and host and can call its methods. Because `AgentClient` doesn't need React, a short Node script using it with a readline loop should give you a working terminal chat. The docs don't describe this setup, so it's my inference rather than a documented workflow. The official `agents-starter` template is a web UI, not a terminal app. Before building your own, it's worth checking the `cloudflare/agents` GitHub repo for a CLI or Node example, since one may have been added recently.\n\nSources:\n- [Cloudflare Agents – Chat client SDK docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/agents/communication-channels/chat/client-sdk/index.md)\n- [Cloudflare Agents docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/agents/index.md)\n- [assistant-ui – Cloudflare Agents integration](https://www.assistant-ui.com/docs/integrations/frameworks/cloudflare-agents/overview)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1181,"cache_read_input_tokens":22300,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1181},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7e1f3cf5-6715-4bd7-afba-50ec633c4977","uuid":"ed1ae2d0-bdc5-4a68-a8a0-587366ff9d11","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:14:05.874Z","request_id":"req_011CfuimQRj5K2HNdSg7TKK8"}
